    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear what you're saying, but it feels like you're applying 21st-century morality to a situation where people had almost no agency. a lot of historians argue that his actions were a calculated, if grim, attempt to maintain some level of french control over domestic affairs so they weren't just governed by a direct military administration. isn't it a bit reductive to just label it \"treason\" when the alternative might have been much more violent for the civilian population?",
