      "content": "The notion that Pétain's actions were a calculated attempt to maintain domestic control is a self-serving revisionist history. Any semblance of \"French control\" under Vichy was merely a facade designed to appease the German occupiers. The reality was that he traded national dignity and democratic principles for a precarious, compromised survival, which is a moral defeat in itself.",
      "source": "target",
